{"id":"exempt-flagged-organizations","title":"Exempt property where flagged organizations are registered","question":"Of the nonprofits that carry warning signs in this project, which are registered at an address the roll shows as exempt, and do any of them no longer hold tax-exempt standing?","finding":"Of 349 flagged nonprofits that could be placed at a San Francisco address, 127 are registered at an address with an institutional exemption on the 2025 roll, $4.06 billion of exempt value between them. 2 of the 6 organizations whose federal exemption was revoked or whose State charity registration is not current are among them: The Gubbio Project (1661 15th St, $519,791; State charity registration: Delinquent); Oakes Childrens Center (98 Bosworth St, $170,208; State charity registration: Delinquent). The largest: California Pacific Medical Center (1101 Van Ness Ave, $2.67 billion); Chinese Hospital Association (845 Jackson St, $245.6 million); Saint Francis Memorial Hospital (900 Hyde St, $157.4 million); SFjazz (201 Franklin St, $72.3 million).","how":"Each flagged nonprofit’s registered address (as placed by the project’s map, from the business register and tax returns) is matched to parcels through the City’s address file, and those parcels are looked up on the 2025 roll. Warning signs are the count carried in the “flagmap” results. Loss of standing comes from the “standing” results: federal revocations and State charity registrations that are not current. Those come first, then by exempt value.","limits":"This is an address match and no more. The roll names no owner: an organization registered at an exempt address may own the building, rent a room in it from a church or another charity, or share it with the exemption’s real holder. A property-tax exemption depends on who owns the property and how it is used, not on who gets mail there. A warning sign elsewhere in this project is a lead, not a finding. What would settle a row: the assessor’s claim file for the parcel, which names the claimant and the use.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"organization","t":"Organization","type":"org"},{"k":"signs","t":"Warning signs","type":"int"},{"k":"strongest","t":"Strongest","type":"text"},{"k":"standing","t":"Standing lost","type":"text"},{"k":"address","t":"Registered address","type":"text"},{"k":"exemption","t":"Exemption on the parcel","type":"text"},{"k":"exempt","t":"Exempt value at the address","type":"usd"},{"k":"parcels","t":"Parcels","type":"int"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid it, fiscal 2019–2026","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"organization":"The Gubbio Project","organizationKey":"GUBBIO PROJECT","signs":7,"strongest":"official finding","standing":"State charity registration: Delinquent","address":"1661 15th St","exemption":"Religious","exempt":519791,"parcels":1,"cityPaid":4738702},{"organization":"Oakes Childrens Center","organizationKey":"OAKES CHILDRENS CENTER","signs":7,"strongest":"official finding","standing":"State charity registration: Delinquent","address":"98 Bosworth St","exemption":"Welfare","exempt":170208,"parcels":1,"cityPaid":6498955},{"organization":"California Pacific Medical Center","organizationKey":"CALIFORNIA PACIFIC MEDICAL CENTER","signs":5,"strongest":"lead","standing":"","address":"1101 Van Ness Ave","exemption":"Welfare","exempt":2666088338,"parcels":1,"cityPaid":1880375},{"organization":"Chinese Hospital Association","organizationKey":"CHINESE HOSPITAL ASSOCIATION","signs":15,"strongest":"lead","standing":"","address":"845 Jackson St","exemption":"Welfare","exempt":245566793,"parcels":1,"cityPaid":53567939},{"organization":"Saint Francis Memorial Hospital","organizationKey":"SAINT FRANCIS MEMORIAL HOSPITAL","signs":6,"strongest":"official finding","standing":"","address":"900 Hyde St","exemption":"Hospital","exempt":157440410,"parcels":1,"cityPaid":0},{"organization":"SFjazz","organizationKey":"SFJAZZ","signs":2,"strongest":"lead","standing":"","address":"201 Franklin St","exemption":"Welfare","exemp